## Why This Is Asked
This question probes practical distributed tracing across Azure services, tenant isolation, and governance at intermediate scale.

## Key Concepts
- Distributed tracing across Front Door, Functions, Event Hubs, Data Lake Gen2, Cosmos/SQL
- OpenTelemetry integration in Azure Functions
- Correlation IDs and per-tenant isolation
- Header preservation and TLS at the edge
- Monitoring with Application Insights and Azure Monitor

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example propagation snippet (conceptual)
import { trace, context, propagation } from '@opentelemetry/api';
export async function handler(req, res) {
  const cid = req.headers['x-correlation-id'] || generateCid();
  req.headers['x-correlation-id'] = cid;
  // bind cid to the active span and propagate downstream
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test trace completeness end-to-end across all components?
- How would you ensure no PII is captured in traces and enforce tenant data boundaries?

## Why This Is Asked

This question validates end-to-end Azure architecture knowledge, including compute, data, observability, security, and disaster recovery fundamentals for a realistic entry-level cloud deployment.

## Key Concepts

- Azure Static Web Apps for SPA hosting with built-in CI/CD
- Azure Functions on Consumption plan for serverless API
- Azure SQL Database with geo-replication for data layer
- Application Insights instrumentation for Functions
- Log Analytics for centralized logging and querying
- Metric alerts for error rate monitoring
- Cost management with budget alerts
- Azure Front Door for TLS termination and global routing
- Basic cross-region DR using redundant services

